  "definition": "Inverter Requirements",
  "effectiveDate": "2020-09-14",
  "historyNote": "#7424, eff 1-12-01; ss by #9353, INTERIM, eff 1-12-09, EXPIRED: 7-11-09 New. #9515, eff 7-18-09; ss by #9998, eff 9-20-11; ss by #13080, eff 9-14-20",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Puc 906.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Puc 906.01 Inverter Requirements",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-07-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 906.01 Inverter Requirements.\n\n(a) A net-metered facility that interconnects to the electric distribution system by means of a single-phase or 3-phase inverter shall be deemed to be compliant with the technical specifications for the facility itself, as established by Puc 900, if the facility complies with the minimum requirements set forth in the following national standards:\n\n(1) The “IEEE Standard 1547 (2018) for Interconnecting Distributed Power Resources with Electric Power Systems” issued by the Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers, Inc., 445 Hoes Lane, Piscataway, New Jersey, available as specified in Appendix B; or\n\n(2) The “UL 1741 SA, Standard for Inverters, Converters, Controllers with Interconnection System Equipment for Use with Distributed Energy Resources,” 2010, issued by Underwriters Laboratories, Inc., 333 Pfingsten Road, Northbrook, Illinois 60062, available as specified in Appendix B.\n\n(b) Each net-metered facility shall be installed in accordance with the State Building Code, including the National Electrical Code, pursuant to RSA 155-A:1, IV, as may be modified from time to time by the state building code review board pursuant to RSA 155-A:10, V.\n\nSource. #7424, eff 1-12-01; ss by #9353, INTERIM, eff 1-12-09, EXPIRED: 7-11-09\n\nNew. #9515, eff 7-18-09; ss by #9998, eff 9-20-11; ss by #13080, eff 9-14-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html"
}
